nodecode-agent-si is a rewrite of joelbrilliant's joelbrilliant/hermes-agent-si:
https://github.com/joelbrilliant/hermes-agent-si
commit adf7abc1d89b1e1ea686ac2fd29e2b95b454f4fe
Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Joel Brilliant (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the three tools (brain_search, brain_get, brain_remember)
and the shapes they answer; the evidence gate that matches a quote against the
user's own messages and refuses one they never typed; the claim model where a
second value disputes a fact instead of overwriting it; the per-turn recall
block; the rule text the model reads; and the session search, over the Claude
Code, Codex and Grok session files on the same machine, as one ranked list
fused by score. What was left out: the vendored engine's change packets,
pending advice and its JSON packet format (the cell keeps claims and notes
directly, which is the part a user sees); its index of Hermes's own state.db
(SQLite), because this cell reads session files and opens no other app's
database; the demo brain, the backup/restore hooks and the background refresh
thread (the index is built at start and on /agent-si index); and the provider
hooks Hermes alone has, replaced by one frame hook and one round hook of
Nodecode's own.
